  <Properties>
    <pitchId>
      <Value><![CDATA[uber-for-nisser]]></Value>
    </pitchId>
    <title>
      <Value><![CDATA[Uber for Elves]]></Value>
    </title>
    <tagline>
      <Value><![CDATA[Your elf is 3 minutes away. He expects porridge.]]></Value>
    </tagline>
    <demoFeatures>
      <Value><![CDATA[Sleigh Tracking
Porridge Tip
Surge Xmas
Attic Pickup]]></Value>
    </demoFeatures>
    <cardsEpic>
      <Value><![CDATA[An elf within 3 minutes of every attic | National coverage by December. The small islands are 'phase 2'.
Disrupt the reindeer monopoly | One man has run Christmas logistics for centuries without a single tender. Time for a platform.
Dynamic porridge pricing | Surge pricing in rice porridge. Christmas Eve: 14 bowls per ride, butter not included.
Elf onboarding at scale | Background checks for 10,000 elves. Every CV says 'mischief, 400 years of experience'.
Attic-to-attic network | Map every loft and crawl space in the country. Street View does not go up there. We do.
Year-round revenue | What do elves do in July? Strategy workshop booked. All the elves declined the invite.]]></Value>
    </cardsEpic>
    <cardsStory>
      <Value><![CDATA[Pay in porridge | As an elf, I want to be paid in rice porridge so that I do not have to prank the household.
Track my elf | As a customer, I want to see my elf on the map so that I know who moved my keys.
Butter tip | As an elf, I want tips as an extra knob of butter so that I feel seen.
Cat-free route | As an elf, I want routes that avoid cats so that I arrive with my hat still on.
Mischief on demand | As a parent, I want to book one small prank so that the kids keep believing.
Surge on the 23rd | As an elf, I want surge pricing on the 23rd so that I can finally afford a taller hat.
Honest rating | As a customer, I want to give 3 stars so that... no, 5 stars. I would like to keep my socks.
Sleigh pooling | As a budget rider, I want to share a sleigh so that I meet new people and their goats.
Quiet ride | As an introverted elf, I want a 'no small talk' option so that I can drive in peace.
Billing for magic | As a PM, I want elves to log their hours so that I can invoice 'magic' at the right rate.
Julefrokost ride home | As a colleague, I want an elf to drive me home from the julefrokost so that I do not attempt the bike.
The nephew wants in | As the client's nephew, I want to be an elf too so that I can 'help out in December'.]]></Value>
    </cardsStory>
    <cardsFeature>
      <Value><![CDATA[Sleigh Tracking | Live map. The icon is a tiny red hat moving through walls.
Porridge Tip | 10%, 15%, or 'the whole pot'.
Surge Xmas | Prices x4 when it snows on Christmas Eve. Unused since 2010.
Attic Pickup | Meet your elf by the box of decorations. He has been there since November.
Hat recognition | Identify your elf by his hat. All the hats are red. Good luck.
Mood filter | Choose your elf: cheerful, mischievous, or 'has not had porridge'.
Lost and found | Everything you lost this year. The elf had it. He is not sorry.
Split the porridge | Share the fare with friends. Somebody always 'forgot their spoon'.
Shelf-sitter seat | One extra passenger dangles off the edge of the sleigh. Free of charge.
Gingerbread loyalty points | Earn one gingerbread per ride. Redeemable for gingerbread.
ETA in sleeps | Arrival time is shown as 'number of sleeps'.
Chimney surcharge | Extra fee for entry by chimney. Elves use the door. Chimneys are the other guy's thing.
Gløgg detector | No driving after gløgg. The sleigh will not start without a breath test.
Pakkeleg dispatch | Send an elf to steal a present from a colleague. Legal says: 'those are the rules of pakkeleg'.
Sock tracking | See which elf has your other sock. Getting it back is a separate, paid feature.
Driver bio | 'Age 412. Likes porridge, dislikes cats. Has been in your attic this whole time.']]></Value>
    </cardsFeature>
    <cardsBug>
      <Value><![CDATA[Elf arrived in June | Timezone bug. He is standing in the garden in wool. Customer confused, elf sweating.
Porridge payment declined | Error: 'insufficient cinnamon'. The elf has started hiding the remote control.
All elves sent to one attic | 847 elves at a single address in Herning. The floor is holding. For now.
Driver is a garden gnome | A gnome accepted the ride. It has not moved. ETA: never. Still rated 4.9 stars.
Ride ends on the roof | GPS thinks every house is a chimney. Customers are stuck. The view is nice.
Elf ate the test data | The seed database was porridge. This one is on us.
Hat invisible in Christmas theme | Red hat on a red background. The elf appears bald. He has filed a complaint.
Everyone booked 24 Dec at 18:00 | The whole country wants the same slot. 'Nobody could have seen this coming,' said nobody.]]></Value>
    </cardsBug>
    <cardsTechdebt>
      <Value><![CDATA[Runs on Santa's old system | A list written in COBOL. It checks itself twice. That is the only test.
elf_new_NEW_use_this_one.dll | Three versions in production. We use the fourth.
Calendar only has December | Months are an enum with one value. Works perfectly one twelfth of the time.
Porridge stored as a string | Portions are text: 'one', 'two', 'a bit more'. Adding them up gives 'NaN porridge'.
The attic is the server room | Hosting is a Raspberry Pi behind the Christmas decorations. Festive, and a fire hazard.
Config in an advent calendar | One setting behind each door. To change the API key, wait until the 17th.]]></Value>
    </cardsTechdebt>
    <cardsCeo>
      <Value><![CDATA[Otto Request: Elves all year | 'Why only December? Think Easter.' Nobody has told the Easter Bunny.
Otto Request: One for tonight? | 'For my speech. Something with a hat.' The entire sprint has been reprioritised.
Otto Request: Premium porridge | 'Like oat milk, but for elves.' Someone wrote it on a sticky note. It is now an epic.]]></Value>
    </cardsCeo>
    <siteHeroHeadline>
      <Value><![CDATA[Your elf is 3 minutes away. Roughly.]]></Value>
    </siteHeroHeadline>
    <siteHeroSub>
      <Value><![CDATA[On-demand elves for every task: gifts, light mischief and attic work. Surge pricing starts on 1 December. Payment in rice porridge only.]]></Value>
    </siteHeroSub>
    <siteCta>
      <Value><![CDATA[Book an elf]]></Value>
    </siteCta>
    <sitePillars>
      <Value><![CDATA[Paid in porridge | No cards, no invoices. One bowl of rice porridge with a knob of butter per ride. Forget the butter and see what happens.
Background-checked | Every elf is vetted for mischief. They all failed. We onboarded them anyway: it is the core feature.
Attic-to-door service | From your attic to wherever the problem is in under ten minutes. Live clog tracking included.]]></Value>
    </sitePillars>
    <siteTestimonials>
      <Value><![CDATA[The elf hid my car keys but arrived on time. Five stars.
We ordered one elf for the julefrokost. Seven showed up. Nobody can find the schnapps.
Surge pricing on Christmas Eve was four bowls of porridge. Worth it.
Mine cancelled twice, then turned up inside the fridge. Ten out of ten, would book again.]]></Value>
    </siteTestimonials>
    <sitePricingJoke>
      <Value><![CDATA[One bowl of porridge per ride. December surge: two bowls plus cinnamon. No butter, no service.]]></Value>
    </sitePricingJoke>
    <siteFooterLine>
      <Value><![CDATA[© Uber for Elves. Drivers are independent nisse contractors. We accept no liability for moved items.]]></Value>
    </siteFooterLine>
